# What an image build of this repository may see — written as an allow-list:
# everything is kept out, then the few paths a build needs are let back in.
# A path that is not named here never reaches a build context, so nothing a
# build cannot see can be copied into a published image: no .env file, no
# .claude/ session state, no edge-function secrets. (Images are published by
# CI from a clean checkout; this is what makes a local build match it.)
#
# The images are in sylou-local/; each adds only the paths it needs.

*

# The Sylou Local web image (sylou-local/web/Dockerfile): the app as Vite
# builds it, from the committed lockfile.
!.npmrc
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!index.html
!vite.config.ts
!tsconfig.json
!tsconfig.app.json
!tsconfig.node.json
!src
!public

# Sylou's licence files, which every image carries in /licenses.
!LICENSE
!LICENSE-METHODOLOGY
!LICENSING.md
!THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md

# The images' own files. Letting one folder back in takes three lines: the
# parent, everything in it out again, then the folders that may be seen.
!sylou-local
sylou-local/*
!sylou-local/web
!sylou-local/functions
!sylou-local/tools
# The licence collector, the licences of the parts that ship none, and the
# package's NOTICE: every image's /licenses.
!sylou-local/licenses
!sylou-local/NOTICE
# The tools image runs these as they are, against the lockfile beside them.
!sylou-local/deno.json
!sylou-local/deno.lock

# The Sylou Local functions image (sylou-local/functions/Dockerfile): the same
# eight functions hosted Sylou deploys, bundled at build time. The build
# deletes the tests and their helper before bundling; this keeps the packages
# the tests install for themselves out of the context altogether.
!supabase
supabase/*
!supabase/functions
supabase/functions/node_modules
# The tools image carries the migrations, so an install can apply them with
# no copy of the repository.
!supabase/migrations

# Hosted Sylou's header file for Cloudflare Pages and Netlify: a package
# install would serve it as a plain file, and its own headers come from
# sylou-local/web/nginx.conf.
public/_headers

# Kept out whatever a line above re-included, because these must never reach
# a build: the last matching pattern wins.
**/.env
**/.env.*
.claude
